WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.139
Before any class goes to a machine, it
has to pass six tests from Chapter 10:

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.447
reachable, deterministic,
bounded, reversible,

3
00:00:08.447 --> 00:00:11.925
verifiable, and not on the
permanently-gated list.

4
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:16.050
With that filter in place, the starting
assignment falls out naturally.

5
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.712
Routine configuration drift and patching
run on machines behind an approval.

6
00:00:20.712 --> 00:00:25.395
Anything critical, or anything
touching authorization or provenance,

7
00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:27.062
halts and goes to a person.

8
00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:29.639
Access requests ride the five clauses,

9
00:00:29.639 --> 00:00:33.424
and an idle entitlement goes
to its owner to decide first.

10
00:00:33.424 --> 00:00:36.475
An agency tunes all of
this in its own record.

11
00:00:36.475 --> 00:00:38.090
Here's the rest of the table.
